  "fighter": {
    "about": "One fighter, flown (src/carrier/fighter.mjs): the same thruster physics as the carrier, in the fighter's own frame. Built for vacuum (tools/blender/fighter_build.py): a crew capsule, two propellant tanks, radiators that fold up instead of wings; `size` is her box without the radiators, which weigh little. 12 t; the main drive gives about 3 g, the manoeuvring clusters about 1 g sideways and a 180\u00b0 turn in about 2 s. `thrusters` places the Blender model's thruster quads and the main drive's force; how she actually flies (the nozzles that push, the tanks, the attitude hold) is `flight`. `landing.lane`: how far out the approach lane's rings run; `ring` their radius; `catch` how close to the gate (m along, m off the line sideways and up) and how slow (m/s) flight control catches a fighter you fly in yourself.",
    "mass": 12000,
    "size": [3.6, 2.2, 10],
    "g": { "about": "What g does to the pilot (src/carrier/gload.mjs). Shift with W is hard burn: the drive's push rises to `boost` times its rating over `spool` seconds, burning propellant to match. Past `tolerate` g the pilot's strain builds at `onset` a second for every g over (times `juiceCut` while the couch's `juice` lasts, seconds of it, topped up on the pad); at 1 she blacks out until it falls back under 0.45; under `tolerate` it falls at `recover` a second.", "boost": 2.7, "spool": 1.2, "tolerate": 4.2, "onset": 0.07, "juiceCut": 0.3, "recover": 0.22, "juice": 60 },
    "com": [0, 0, 0],
    "thrusters": {
      "main": [{ "at": [0, 0, 3.9], "r": 0.75, "force": 3.6e5 }],
      "rcsForce": 3.0e4,
      "rcs": [
        { "at": [-1.15, 0.5, -3.4] }, { "at": [1.15, 0.5, -3.4] }, { "at": [-1.15, -0.5, -3.4] }, { "at": [1.15, -0.5, -3.4] },
        { "at": [-1.15, 0.5, 3.4] }, { "at": [1.15, 0.5, 3.4] }, { "at": [-1.15, -0.5, 3.4] }, { "at": [1.15, -0.5, 3.4] }
      ]
    },
    "flight": {
      "about": "How she flies (src/carrier/flight.mjs), as signed off in the Fighter Sound Lab: Newton only, no drag, no top speed, no drift kill. `hold`: the drive lights at `rampFrom` of full power and ramps at `rampRate` a second while W is held; the aim may lead the nose by `lead` rad; `sens` rad a mouse pixel; `keyRate` / `rollRate` the turn the arrows and Z C ask for (rad/s); `wmax` the hold's cruise turn rate per axis (pitch, yaw, roll); `minPop` the smallest pop as a fraction of a second of full jets; `gap` the beat between pops. `inertia` (kg m\u00b2) and `com` in her model's frame. `blocks`: the four jet blocks (bow and stern at the height of the centre of mass, so a slide is a pure slide and a yaw a pure yaw), `pan` for the sound. `nozzles`: [id, block, the way the gas goes, `force` kind, metres out from the block]. `alloc`: per command (slide right, rise, back (retro), pitch up, yaw left, roll left) the nozzles each way. `opposed`: pairs that would cancel, so neither opens. `tank` kg and `isp` s: 3 t of torch-drive propellant and 1.2 t of cold gas (about 250 m/s of sliding). `nozzle`: the drive's mouth.",
      "hold": { "rampFrom": 0.3, "rampRate": 0.45, "lead": 0.6, "sens": 0.0024, "keyRate": 0.8, "rollRate": 1.2, "wmax": [1.4, 1.1, 2.0], "minPop": 0.03, "gap": 0.06 },
      "inertia": [116000, 146000, 42000],
      "com": [0, 0.2, -0.35],
      "nozzle": [0, 0, 4.5],
      "tank": { "main": 3000, "rcs": 1200 },
      "isp": { "main": 2000, "rcs": 300 },
      "force": { "rcs": 30000, "tip": 18000 },
      "blocks": [
