  "weapons": {
    "about": "The carrier's guns, her point defence and her torpedoes, and the raider that attacks her (src/carrier/weapons.mjs). There are no shields: what keeps a ship alive is armour (`integrity.armour`), point defence, and not being where the shot is aimed. `turrets`: each heavy turret is a `mount` (its id, also the name of its gunhouse in hull.glb, and `<id>-guns` its barrels), fed from its `magazine` compartment up its `barbette`; `from` is the hatch you man it from (deck, spot, the way you face when you leave). `gun`, for every turret: `shell` muzzle speed m/s, `reload` seconds per barrel, `crewReload` the same for a turret its crew fires, `train` and `elevate` the fastest it turns (degrees a second), `elevation` its limits (degrees, toward the side the turret stands on), `rack` rounds in the ready rack, `stock` rounds in the magazine, `hoist` seconds to send one round up, `spread` the aim error of a shot (radians), `crewSpread` how far off a crew lays the guns, `range` metres a shell flies, `damage` what one does to the raider's hull, `fouled` metres of line of fire checked against the hull, `heat` what one shot puts into the ship's heat sinks (0 to 1 of them). `pdc`: the point defence cannons, rotary guns on the layout's `pdc` mounts, run by the fire-control computer: each one takes the nearest torpedo (or, with none, the raider inside `raiderRange`) that is within `range` and `arc` degrees of where the mount faces, leads it (for its acceleration too), slews at `slew` degrees a second and fires `rate` tracers a second (each tracer stands for a burst of rounds) at `speed` m/s, off by `spread` radians; a tracer passing within `radius` metres of a torpedo kills it, and one that meets the raider does `damage`. `stock` is the tracers each mount's magazine holds (its `magazine` in the mounts), `heat` what each tracer puts into the sinks. A mount is as healthy as the compartment it is fixed to. `torpedo`: every torpedo, either side's: `accel` m/s² for `burn` seconds, launched at `push` m/s, gone after `life` seconds; `jink` m/s² of random weave once it is within `terminal` metres (what makes point defence miss); `fuse` metres from its target it goes off. Into the carrier it does `pen`, `damage` and `hole` as a shell does (integrity.mjs), never stopped by the armour; into the raider, `raiderDamage`. `tubes`: the carrier's own torpedo tubes, fired by the CIC at a raider between `range` metres: `salvo` at a time, `every` seconds, from `magazine` while it holds `stock`, out of the hull at `at` (ship frame) along `dir`. `raider`: its `hull` (armour and all), `speed` (m/s past the carrier) and `accel`, `jink` (m/s² of evasive weave, changing every second or two: what makes a long shot miss), `standoff` (the range of its passes, metres), `passes`, `size` (half-axes of the ellipsoid shells hit), its `gun` (`shell` m/s, seconds `every` between shots, `spread`, `range`), its `torpedo` launches (a `salvo` every `every` seconds while the carrier is between `range` metres, `stock` in all), its own point defence `pdc` against the carrier's torpedoes (`range`, `rate`, `spread`, `speed`), and its `flak` at a fighter within `range`: a shot `every` so many seconds at `shell` m/s, aimed where she will be if she flies on as she is, off by up to `spread` radians, doing `damage` if it passes within `radius` metres of her. `target`: the gunnery drill's sled, towed `tow` metres astern of a tug on `passes` straight passes `standoff` metres off at `speed`; `size` is the ellipsoid a shell must pass through to score, `clear` how far off the tug is gone. It has no hull to lose: hits are counted. `fighter`: the fighter's twin cannon: `shell` m/s on top of her own velocity, seconds `every` between rounds, `spread`, `range` metres a round flies, `rounds` in the drum (refilled on the pad), the `damage` one round does to a raider (or a torpedo, within `radius`), and her own `hull` (mended on the pad; at nothing she is dead in space and flight control brings her in). `railgun`: the spinal gun along the keel, fired from the helm (F): it points where the ship points, so you aim it by turning her. A slug leaves at `speed` m/s on top of her velocity, off by `spread`; the capacitors take `charge` seconds to fill (on main power only) and each shot puts `heat` into the sinks; a slug that meets the raider does `damage`, and it is gone after `range` metres. `stock` slugs; the muzzle is at `muzzle` (ship frame).",
    "turrets": [
      { "mount": "turret-dorsal", "name": "Dorsal turret", "barbette": "dorsal-barbette", "magazine": "magazine", "from": { "deck": 2, "at": [12.7, -24], "yaw": 1.5708, "label": "Climb the hoist trunk to the dorsal turret" } },
      { "mount": "turret-ventral", "name": "Ventral turret", "barbette": "ventral-barbette", "magazine": "magazine-fwd", "from": { "deck": 2, "at": [0, -80], "yaw": 0, "label": "Climb down to the ventral turret" } }
    ],
    "gun": { "shell": 1400, "reload": 1.6, "crewReload": 4.2, "train": 28, "elevate": 20, "elevation": [-6, 82], "rack": 24, "stock": 260, "hoist": 2.5, "spread": 0.0012, "crewSpread": 0.02, "range": 4200, "damage": [26, 40], "fouled": 320, "heat": 0.004 },
